# Indexed prices over time. Figures are a percentage.
# 100% = the price specified in the .dat file (adjusted for meters per tile and bits per month)
# If any of the types are not specified, the "general" type will be used.

# General taken from https://www.officialdata.org/uk/inflation/1900?amount=1
# All calibrated to 1900 as 100%
# Last updated: 2026-11-15 (general to 2026 actuals with 2027-2050 projected;
# passenger fare rebased to the ONS series and extended to 2050; corporation
# tax and base rate brought up to date and held forward).
# 2021 and 2022 corrected on that date: the old 2022 entry (13096) predated the
# 9.1% CPI outturn for that year. 2021-2025 are from the source above; 2026 is
# provisional, from the ONS CPI quarterly rates (3.0% annual average), because the
# source's own 2026 forecast of 0.93% is stale against the 3.5% rate now reported.
# Forward path: 4.5% for 2027 and 3.0% for 2028 (the Bank of England expects about
# 5% in mid-2027 before it falls back), 2.5% for 2029, then the 2.0% inflation
# target from 2030, carried to 2050 and shown at five-year intervals so that the
# linear interpolation stays close to the compounding.
# Figures for wages are in staff.tab
# TODO: Get bespoke figures here for the specific types not yet completed.

